flowchart TB
  accTitle: How the Canary runs the path of an issue through the AI
  accDescr: The Canary starts every Monday, after a change on main of the script, the prompts, the action, the reusable workflow, the firewall policy, the settings or the canary's issue, and by hand. It calls the reusable workflow as every repository does, with the permissions of the template, the engine's secrets passed by name and the input canary. Its job event takes the canary's issue and sets no labels; outside this repository, or when the called workflow doesn't see the variable ISSUE_ASSISTANT_AI set to on, the canary fails. Its job analyze runs on the firewall runner with the engine's secret of the environment issue-assistant, context reads the issue of tests/fixtures/canary-issue.json instead of one on GitHub, and the engine answers with JSON. Without the secret or without an answer, the canary fails. Its job apply checks the answer as for a real issue, as a dry run: an answer that breaks a check fails the canary, and one that passes shows the comment it would post in the summary. Beside the call, its job the AI's wait for its runner reads the jobs of the run until analyze starts: it warns when analyze waited for more than 10 minutes, and when it waits for more than 30, the canary fails and opens the issue of the bot-health bot at once.
  start(["every Monday, a change<br>on main, or by hand"]) --> caller
  caller["`**the call of the template**:<br>its permissions, the secrets<br>by name, canary: true`"] --> event
  event["`**event**: the canary's issue,<br>no labels`"] --> seen{"this repository,<br>ISSUE_ASSISTANT_AI on?"}
  seen -- "no" --> red["the canary fails:<br>no release"]
  seen -- "yes" --> analyze
  fixture[("tests/fixtures/<br>canary-issue.json")] --> analyze
  analyze["`**analyze**: the firewall runner,<br>the secret of the environment,<br>the engine`"] --> answered{"a secret and a<br>structured answer?"}
  answered -- "no" --> red
  answered -- "yes" --> apply["`**apply**, a dry run:<br>the checks of every answer`"]
  apply -- "a check fails" --> red
  apply -- "it passes" --> green["the comment it would post,<br>in the summary"]
  start --> queue["`**the AI's wait for its runner**:<br>beside the call, a warning<br>above 10 minutes`"]
  queue -- "analyze waits over 30 minutes:<br>an issue of bot-health at once" --> red
  classDef trigger fill:#d4a72c33,stroke:#bf8700,stroke-width:2px
  classDef ai fill:#8250df33,stroke:#8250df,stroke-width:2px
  classDef job fill:#8c959f1f,stroke:#8c959f,stroke-width:2px
  classDef safe fill:#1a7f3726,stroke:#1a7f37,stroke-width:2px
  classDef untrusted fill:#cf222e26,stroke:#cf222e,stroke-width:2px
  class start,fixture,seen,answered trigger
  class analyze ai
  class caller,event,apply,queue job
  class green safe
  class red untrusted
